  "verbalization": "Ammonium lactate exhibits a potential relationship with seborrheic dermatitis through a chain of indications involving benzoyl peroxide, which in turn links to the condition. The evidence suggests that Ammonium lactate may be associated with contact dermatitis and granuloma annulare, both of which are linked to seborrheic dermatitis via benzoyl peroxide. This implies a possible indirect pathway where Ammonium lactate could influence the development of seborrheic dermatitis through the action of benzoyl peroxide, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, but further investigation is needed to establish a direct causal link. The presence of multiple indirect pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship and underscores the need for additional mechanistic studies to clarify the role of Ammonium lactate in seborrheic dermatitis.",
